<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item11> a pr:CodeTraceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Direct ;
    en:normStem "" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 3 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_29>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_38> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP3.03> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 3 ;
    pr:chapter 3 ;
    pr:code """tags = ['v28.0', 'v3.1', 'v28.0rc1',
        'v4.0', 'v24.2', 'v9.1']
final = [t for t in tags if 'rc' not in t]
def key(t):
    return [int(p) for p in t[1:].split('.')]
a = sorted(final)
b = sorted(final, key=key)
move = 0
for t in final:
    move += abs(a.index(t) - b.index(t))
print(move)""" ;
    pr:codeLines 11 ;
    pr:codeMaxColumns 45 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt1:i11:trace-release-tags" ;
    pr:itemType pr:CodeTrace ;
    pr:keyOutput "12" ;
    pr:position 11 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src11> ;
    pr:stem "A script lists release tags, drops the release candidates (their tag carries rc), and compares the order of the final releases sorted as text with the order sorted by version number. It adds up how far each tag moves between the two orders. What does it print?" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12> a pr:ChoiceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Synthesis ;
    en:normStem "anodesconfigurationfileholdsanrpcauthlineandap2pkhoutputscriptholdsa20bytehashofapublickeybothkeepahashinsteadofthesecretwhichstatementcomparesthemcorrectly" ;
    en:optionSetKey "aleakofthefilerevealsnopasswordbecausetherpcauthhashissaltedthep2pkhhashisacommitmenttothekeyandthekeyisrevealedonlywhenthecoinsarespent|aleakofthefilerevealsthepasswordatoncebecauserpcauthisonlyanencodingthep2pkhhashisrevealedtogetherwiththekeywhentheoutputiscreated|bothhashesaresaltedchecksumsthatcatchtyposandbothsecretsarerevealedassoonasanodereadsthelineorthescript|therpcauthhashisacommitmentthattheownerrevealswhenthecoinsarespentthep2pkhhashissaltedsoaleakofthescriptrevealsnokey" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 3 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_130>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch03_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_131>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch04_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_79>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch04_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_92> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP3.08>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP4.05> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 4 ;
    pr:chapter 3,
        4 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt1:i12:rpcauth-and-p2pkh" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFour ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optD> ;
    pr:position 12 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src12> ;
    pr:stem "A node's configuration file holds an rpcauth line, and a P2PKH output script holds a 20-byte hash of a public key. Both keep a hash instead of the secret. Which statement compares them correctly?" ;
    pr:synthesis true .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "Both hashes are salted checksums that catch typos, and both secrets are revealed as soon as a node reads the line or the script." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optB> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "A leak of the file reveals no password, because the rpcauth hash is salted; the P2PKH hash is a commitment to the key, and the key is revealed only when the coins are spent." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "A leak of the file reveals the password at once, because rpcauth is only an encoding; the P2PKH hash is revealed together with the key when the output is created." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item12_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "The rpcauth hash is a commitment that the owner reveals when the coins are spent; the P2PKH hash is salted, so a leak of the script reveals no key." .

