<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15> a pr:ChoiceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Synthesis ;
    en:normStem "danascoinsweresenttotheaddressthatcomesfromthecompressedpublickeyofherprivatekeyherpaperbackupholdsthatprivatekeyinwifbutthiswifhasnofinal01byteanewwalletimportsitandshowsazerobalancewhichdiagnosisfitsandwhichcheckbeforefundingwouldhavecaughtit" ;
    en:optionSetKey "thecoinsweresenttoanaddresswithnokeybehinditbecauseavalidchecksumdoesnotprovethatakeyexistscheckingthechecksumoftheaddressagainwouldhavecaughtit|themissingbytechangedtheprivatekeyitselfsoitcannolongerproduceherpublickeyatallonlyasecondwrittencopyofthepaperwouldhavecaughtit|theversionbyte80marksatestnetworkkeysothewalletlooksforhercoinsonanothernetworksendingaverysmallamountfirstandwaitingadaywouldhavecaughtit|thewallettookthekeyasuncompressedandwatchestheotheraddressofthesamekeyrestoringfromthepaperandcomparingthefirstaddresswiththeprintedonebeforeanycoinsweresentwouldhavecaughtit" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 4 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch04_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_46>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch04_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_61>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch04_quiz_v1_0_0_json_2>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch05_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_113> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP4.09>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP4.10>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP4.13>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP5.07> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 4 ;
    pr:chapter 4,
        5 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt1:i14:wif-flag-and-balance" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFour ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optD> ;
    pr:position 15 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src15> ;
    pr:stem "Dana's coins were sent to the address that comes from the compressed public key of her private key. Her paper backup holds that private key in WIF, but this WIF has no final 01 byte. A new wallet imports it and shows a zero balance. Which diagnosis fits, and which check before funding would have caught it?" ;
    pr:synthesis true .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "The missing byte changed the private key itself, so it can no longer produce her public key at all; only a second written copy of the paper would have caught it." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optB> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "The version byte 80 marks a test network key, so the wallet looks for her coins on another network; sending a very small amount first and waiting a day would have caught it." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "The coins were sent to an address with no key behind it, because a valid checksum does not prove that a key exists; checking the checksum of the address again would have caught it." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item15_optD> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "The wallet took the key as uncompressed and watches the other address of the same key; restoring from the paper and comparing the first address with the printed one, before any coins were sent, would have caught it." .

