    pr:position 18 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src18> ;
    pr:stem "Lena's phone is stolen. She restores her wallet from her twelve-word recovery code on a new phone. The wallet opens with different addresses, an empty balance and none of her labels. She had set a passphrase in the old wallet and had exported her labels in the BIP329 format. What is the most complete explanation and the fix?" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item18_optA> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "A passphrase forks the wallet, so the same twelve words without it give a different wallet, and labels cannot be derived from the seed; she must enter the passphrase and import the labels file." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item18_optB> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "The recovery code was stored on the stolen phone, so the thief has already spent the coins and nothing can be restored." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item18_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "The gap limit stopped the scan too early; a larger gap limit would bring back both the balance and the labels." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item18_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "Labels are derived from the seed and were lost with the phone, while the passphrase only changes how the twelve words are spelled, so nothing else is missing." .

