    pr:itemKey "mt1:i23:tracker-legacy-vs-segwit" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFour ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optD> ;
    pr:position 23 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src23> ;
    pr:stem "A payment tracker identifies each withdrawal by its txid. Before two withdrawals confirm, a stranger changes one of them: for a legacy payment the stranger re-encodes the signature inside the input script, and for a segwit payment the stranger changes only the signature bytes in the witness. Both payments stay valid. Which outcome is right?" ;
    pr:synthesis true .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "Both payments keep their txid, because a signature is never part of any hash of the transaction." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optB> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "The legacy payment gets a new txid, so the tracker may believe it failed; the segwit payment keeps its txid, because the witness lies outside the txid." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "The legacy payment keeps its txid and the segwit payment gets a new one, because the txid covers the extended serialization." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item23_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "Both payments get a new txid, so the tracker must follow the wtxid of every payment." .

