    pr:itemKey "mt1:i01:gox-two-events" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFour ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optD> ;
    pr:position 4 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src4> ;
    pr:stem "The course tells two stories about the exchange Mt. Gox in 2014. On 28 February it filed for bankruptcy after admitting that about 850,000 bitcoin were gone. Three weeks later it said it had found about 200,000 bitcoin in an old-format wallet file that it believed was empty. Which statement says correctly what each story teaches?" ;
    pr:synthesis true .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optA> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "The filing: customers held balances on a website while the keys were in other hands, so whoever holds the keys holds the coins; the old file: a wallet file can still hold spendable keys, so an untested file is not an empty one." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optB> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "The filing: an untested backup file is not an empty one; the old file: whoever holds the keys holds the coins, exchanges included." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "The filing: the network let the exchange spend the same coins twice; the old file: miners had held the coins back until the exchange paid a larger fee." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item4_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "The filing: customers lost their own keys while writing down a recovery code; the old file: backups expire, so an old wallet file can safely be thrown away." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5> a pr:ChoiceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Synthesis ;
    en:normStem "theprogramappliestwotransactionstoasetofunspentoutputsthatstartsat80satoshisintotalwhatdoesitprintandwhatexplainsthetotalutxoa050b130defapplyinsoutstxidforiininsdelutxoifornvinenumerateoutsutxotxidstrnvapplya02029capplyc0b145dprintsortedutxosumutxovalues" ;
    en:optionSetKey "a0b1c0c1d0174spentoutputsstayinthesetandeverynewoutputisadded|c1d074the6satoshisthataremissingarechangethatwasnevercreated|c1d074the6satoshisthataremissingarethefeesofthetwotransactions|c1d080spendingmovesvaluetonewoutputsbutneverremovesany" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 2 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch02_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_60>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch06_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_53> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP2.11>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP2.14>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP6.09> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 4 ;
    pr:chapter 2,
        6 ;
    pr:code """utxo = {'a:0': 50, 'b:1': 30}
def apply(ins, outs, txid):
    for i in ins:
        del utxo[i]
    for n, v in enumerate(outs):
        utxo[txid + ':' + str(n)] = v
apply(['a:0'], [20, 29], 'c')
apply(['c:0', 'b:1'], [45], 'd')
print(sorted(utxo), sum(utxo.values()))""" ;
    pr:codeLines 9 ;
    pr:codeMaxColumns 39 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt1:i08:utxo-set-trace" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFourCode ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optD> ;
    pr:position 5 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src5> ;
    pr:stem "The program applies two transactions to a set of unspent outputs that starts at 80 satoshis in total. What does it print, and what explains the total?" ;
    pr:synthesis true .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "['a:0', 'b:1', 'c:0', 'c:1', 'd:0'] 174 : spent outputs stay in the set and every new output is added" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optB> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "['c:1', 'd:0'] 80 : spending moves value to new outputs but never removes any" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "['c:1', 'd:0'] 74 : the 6 satoshis that are missing are change that was never created" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item5_optD> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "['c:1', 'd:0'] 74 : the 6 satoshis that are missing are the fees of the two transactions" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6> a pr:ChoiceItem,
        pr:Item ;
    en:copyChecked true ;
    en:kind en:Direct ;
    en:normStem "" ;
    en:optionSetKey "theshopisequallysafeatsixconfirmationsagainsteitherattackerbecauseeveryconfirmationdividesthechancebythesamefactor|theshopneedsthreeconfirmationsagainstthe10percentattackerbuttenagainstthe30percentattacker|threeconfirmationsareenoughagainstthe30percentattackerbecausethechancefallsbelow5percentoncezreachestheattackersshare|twoconfirmationsareenoughagainstthe10percentattackerbecausethefigureforz2isbelow5percent" ;
    en:origin en:Authored ;
    en:primaryChapter 2 ;
    en:seedItem <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch02_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_140>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch02_question_bank_v1_0_0_json_143>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/page#ch02_quiz_v1_0_0_json_3> ;
    en:tests <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/criticalpoint#CP2.05> ;
    pr:bloomLevel 4 ;
    pr:chapter 2 ;
    pr:itemKey "mt1:i07:shop-confirmations" ;
    pr:itemType pr:ChoiceFour ;
    pr:option <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optA>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optB>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optC>,
        <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optD> ;
    pr:position 6 ;
    pr:source <http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_src6> ;
    pr:stem "The chapter recomputes the white paper's table: the chance, in percent, that an attacker who holds a share of the hash power ever catches up when a payment has z confirmations. For an attacker with 10 percent: z = 1 gives 20.5, z = 2 gives 5.1, z = 3 gives 1.3 and z = 6 gives 0.02. For an attacker with 30 percent: z = 1 gives 62.8, z = 3 gives 32.5, z = 6 gives 13.2, z = 9 gives 5.5 and z = 10 gives 4.2. A shop accepts a payment only when the chance of a reversal is below 5 percent. Which statement follows from these figures?" .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optA> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "A" ;
    pr:text "Two confirmations are enough against the 10 percent attacker, because the figure for z = 2 is below 5 percent." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optB> pr:isKey true ;
    pr:letter "B" ;
    pr:text "The shop needs three confirmations against the 10 percent attacker but ten against the 30 percent attacker." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optC> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "C" ;
    pr:text "Three confirmations are enough against the 30 percent attacker, because the chance falls below 5 percent once z reaches the attacker's share." .

<http://example.org/sen0401/engine/paper#midterm_v1_item6_optD> pr:isKey false ;
    pr:letter "D" ;
    pr:text "The shop is equally safe at six confirmations against either attacker, because every confirmation divides the chance by the same factor." .

